{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "Liam woke up to the sound of birds chirping in a synthetic forest, the air thick with the scent of pixelated flowers. His vision blurred for a moment before sharpening into crisp, blocky clarity. He looked down at his hands—his fingers were now rendered in low-poly 3D, his pajamas replaced by a pixelated tunic. Panic surged as he realized the world around him was a grid of repeating textures, NPCs frozen mid-step like broken marionettes. A floating text box appeared before him, reading *\"Welcome to Pixelia! Objective: Find the Golden Key to unlock the next level.\"* He stumbled forward, his footsteps echoing unnaturally, as the ground beneath him rippled like an old CRT screen.\n\n***\n\nLiam sprinted through a village of chibi-like characters, their voices reduced to 8-bit blips. A quest giver NPC, his face locked in a perpetual grin, thrust a sword into his hands and barked, *\"Slay the Pixel Wyrm in the cave!\"* The cave entrance yawned ahead, its jagged edges too symmetrical to be natural. As Liam stepped inside, the walls pulsed with light, and his HUD flickered with a warning: *\"Health: 100/100. Warning: Death in-game resets progress.\"* His heart pounded—he had to escape, but how? The exit glitched in and out of existence, the game’s code glaringly visible beneath the surface. With a deep breath, he raised the sword, the weight of pixels heavier than any real steel. The Wyrm’s roar shook the cavern, and Liam knew: this was no dream.", "logprobs": [{"token": "L", "logprob": -1.9598238468170166}, {"token": "iam", "logprob": -0.00010692501382436603}, {"token": " woke", "logprob": -1.5613118410110474}, {"token": " up", "logprob": -0.549272894859314}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.09323673695325851}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.01384382601827383}, {"token": " sound", "logprob": -0.2412261962890625}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.529